hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1639","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Hisham and Yahya ibn Hakim—this is the narration of Yahya—both said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, who said: Narrated to us Shu'bah, from Ayyub, from Abu al-'Aliyah al-Bara', from 'Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr (RA), from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said:\n\n\How will you be when you remain among a people who delay the prayer from its appointed time?\""\n\nAbu Dharr (RA) said to him: \""Pray the prayer at its appointed time. Then"," if you catch them having not prayed"," pray with them"," and do not say"," 'I have already prayed"," so I will not pray.'\""\n\nBundar did not narrate the phrase: \""Pray the prayer at its appointed time.\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
